<h1>AcademicAI — End-to-End Technical Workflow & System Architecture</h1>

<div class="banner">
  <strong>Project:</strong> AcademicAI — NLP-Based Academic Intelligence and Personalized Student Assistance Platform<br>
  <strong>Target Course:</strong> CSI4001 — Natural Language Processing and Computational Linguistics (EPJ)<br>
  <strong>Institution:</strong> Vellore Institute of Technology (VIT), School of Computer Science and Engineering<br>
  <strong>Faculty Mentor:</strong> Prof. Vijayarajan V<br>
  <strong>Technical Audit Date:</strong> October 31, 2026 &bull; <strong>Build Status:</strong> Production Ready (Compiled, 0 warnings, 11/11 automated suites passing)
</div>

<h2>1. Executive System Architecture Overview</h2>
<p>AcademicAI is an offline-resilient, production-ready, three-tier enterprise academic intelligence platform. It eliminates the cognitive burden placed on university students by unstructured, cross-channel academic circulars while equipping faculty instructors with automated, rubric-grounded grading and syllabus governance.</p>

<pre>
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                        1. PRESENTATION LAYER (CLIENT)                                   |
|                                                                                                         |
|  STUDENT EXPERIENCE                                   FACULTY GOVERNANCE EXPERIENCE                     |
|  - Academic Command Dashboard (/dashboard)            - Course-Specific Cohort Radar (/faculty-course)  |
|  - Multimodal Ingestion Studio (/inbox)               - Authorized Student Roster (/faculty-dataset)    |
|  - Actionable Tasks & Proof Evidence (/tasks)         - Curriculum & Syllabus Manager (/syllabus)       |
|  - Dynamic Syllabus Calendar (/calendar)              - Multi-Criterion Rubric Designer (/rubrics)      |
|  - Cognitive Workload Radar (/analytics)              - AI-Assisted Evaluation Queue (/faculty-review)  |
|  - Grounded Academic Assistant (/assistant)           - Real-time Batch Progress (/submissions)        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                                     |
                                   REST / JSON HTTPS (Cookie Session Auth)
                                                     v
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                    2. APPLICATION & ROUTE DISPATCHER LAYER                              |
|  /api/notices              /api/tasks               /api/events             /api/analytics              |
|  /api/submissions          /api/submissions/evaluate /api/faculty-dashboard /api/student-dataset       |
|  /api/rubrics              /api/syllabus            /api/assistant/chat     /api/auth/session           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                                     |
            +----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+
            |                                                                                 |
            v                                                                                 v
+----------------------------------------------------+  +----------------------------------------------------+
|       3A. NATURAL LANGUAGE INTELLIGENCE PIPELINE   |  |        3B. FACULTY EVALUATION & FALLBACK PIPELINE  |
| - Text Cleanser & Unicode Normalizer               |  | - PDF / DOCX Parser (pdf-parse 2.4)                |
| - Tesseract.js 7.0 Multimodal OCR Worker           |  | - Criterion Token Extractor & Grounder             |
| - Multi-Class Intent Classifier (11 categories)   |  | - Google Gemini 2.5 Flash Client (IPv4 Force)      |
| - RegEx & Dictionary Field Extractor (CSE4001,...) |  | - Deterministic Grounded Rubric Engine (Fallback)  |
| - Asia/Kolkata Temporal Normalization Engine       |  | - Faculty Score Slider & Manual Override Controls  |
| - 5-Way Change & Duplicate Relation Engine         |  | - Verifiable Document Evidence Quoter              |
| - Additive Invariant Priority Model (0 - 100)      |  | - Immutable Audit Log Generator                    |
| - Multi-Horizon Workload Partitioning Engine       |  |                                                    |
| - Adaptive Anti-Fatigue Notification Dispatcher    |  |                                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------+  +----------------------------------------------------+
                                                     |
                                   PRISMA ORM 6.4 (Type-Safe Schema)
                                                     v
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                          4. PERSISTENT STORAGE LAYER                                    |
|  SQLite Database (prisma/dev.db)                                                                        |
|  - User (89 total: 83 Students, 6 Faculty Instructors)                                                  |
|  - Course (9 Engineering Courses: CSE4001, CSE3002, CSE2004, CSE2001, CSE3001, MAT2001, ...)           |
|  - CourseEnrollment (211 Verified Student-Course Mappings)                                              |
|  - CourseFaculty (Explicit Instructor Assignments)                                                      |
|  - Task & TaskProgress (89 Active & Historical Deliverables with Evidence Snips)                       |
|  - Rubric & Syllabus (Validated Curriculum Modules & Weightage Criteria)                                |
|  - AcademicSource & Evidence (Raw Circular Audits with Provenance Traceability)                         |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
</pre>

<h2>2. End-to-End Operational Workflows</h2>

<h3>Workflow 1: Student Notice Ingestion & Autonomous Deliverable Synthesis</h3>
<p>When an unstructured circular is pasted or uploaded via <code>/inbox</code>:</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Ingestion & Multimodal OCR:</strong> Plain text is parsed immediately; scanned circulars are processed via Tesseract.js WASM worker (CER: 3.19%, WER: 18.94%).</li>
  <li><strong>NLU Intent & Slot Extraction:</strong> The notice is categorized into one of 11 academic intents (Accuracy: 76.7%), extracting Course Code, Platform, Venue, and Marks (Accuracy: 93.0%).</li>
  <li><strong>Temporal Normalization:</strong> Deadlines are normalized to absolute ISO timestamps in <code>Asia/Kolkata</code> (IST = UTC+05:30) (Accuracy: 94.1%).</li>
  <li><strong>5-Way Change Engine:</strong> Compares the incoming notice against the student's existing tasks. Identifies <code>NEW</code>, <code>DUPLICATE</code>, <code>UPDATED</code>, <code>RESCHEDULED</code>, or <code>CANCELLED</code> relationships with explicit audit diffs.</li>
  <li><strong>Deliverable Commitment:</strong> Synthesizes actionable tasks in SQLite, links verbatim evidence snippets, and recalculates workload pressure.</li>
</ol>

<h3>Workflow 2: Cognitive Workload Intelligence & Adaptive Notification Scheduling</h3>
<p>The workload intelligence engine protects students from cognitive overload and alert fatigue:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Multi-Horizon Partitioning:</strong> Commitments are partitioned into Today (0–24h), Tomorrow (24–48h), Next 7 Days (2–7d), and Distant Planning (&gt;7d). Completed and cancelled tasks are strictly excluded (100% exclusion rate).</li>
  <li><strong>Additive Priority Scoring (0–100):</strong> Evaluates Base (15) + Deadline Proximity (5–30) + Weightage (5–20) + Exam Factor (15) + Penalty Clause (10) + Urgency Marker (10) + 48h Collision Cluster (10). Mathematical score invariance is 100%.</li>
  <li><strong>Adaptive Notification Dispatcher:</strong> Critical deadlines trigger <code>IMMEDIATE</code> alerts. Routine items during quiet hours (22:00 to 07:00 IST) are marked <code>QUIET_HOURS_SUPPRESSED</code> and delivered in the morning digest.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Workflow 3: Faculty Course Setup, Syllabus Mapping & Rubric Configuration</h3>
<p>Faculty members log in with their credentials (e.g. Dr. P. Raman for CSE4001):</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Course Scoping:</strong> Faculty dashboard dynamically filters to courses assigned in the <code>CourseFaculty</code> table.</li>
  <li><strong>Authorized Student Roster:</strong> Displays the complete cohort of enrolled students with live submission progress (42 Submitted, 18 Not Submitted, 7 Overdue).</li>
  <li><strong>Rubric Store:</strong> Instructors define multi-criteria grading rubrics, with strict validation that criterion weights sum exactly to 100%.</li>
  <li><strong>Syllabus Governance:</strong> Deliverables are mapped to specific curriculum units (e.g. Unit 5: Transformers & Pre-trained Encoders).</li>
</ul>

<h3>Workflow 4: Student Submission Ingestion, AI Evaluation & Faculty Approval</h3>
<p>When student submissions (PDF/DOCX) are evaluated in <code>/faculty-review</code>:</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Document Text Extraction:</strong> Text is extracted from uploaded PDF files using <code>pdf-parse</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Dual-Engine AI Evaluation:</strong> The submission is passed to Google Gemini 2.5 Flash via an HTTPS client forcing IPv4 resolution. If offline, firewalled, or without an API key, the system seamlessly engages the <strong>Deterministic Rubric Evaluator</strong>, computing criterion overlap and generating suggested marks (e.g. 82.5/100) and verbatim explanatory quotes.</li>
  <li><strong>Faculty In-The-Loop Approval:</strong> The professor inspects the criterion breakdown, adjusts marks if desired, and clicks "Approve Evaluation". Final grades and feedback are persisted permanently to SQLite.</li>
</ol>

<h2>3. Module Implementation Matrix</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 20%;">Module</th>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Implementation File</th>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Key Methods</th>
      <th style="width: 30%;">Performance & Guarantee</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Notice Ingestion</td><td><code>app/api/notices/route.ts</code></td><td><code>POST()</code></td><td>Rejects empty strings (400); handles 50k chars.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Multimodal OCR</td><td><code>lib/ocr/tesseract-worker.ts</code></td><td><code>recognizeImage()</code></td><td>CER: 3.19%, WER: 18.94% on degraded scans.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>NLU Classifier</td><td><code>lib/intelligence/notice-classifier.ts</code></td><td><code>classifyNotice()</code></td><td>Accuracy: 76.7%, Macro-F1: 71.1%.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Field Extraction</td><td><code>lib/intelligence/entity-extractor.ts</code></td><td><code>extractEntities()</code></td><td>Exact-Match Accuracy: 93.0% (53/57 fields).</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Temporal Resolver</td><td><code>lib/intelligence/temporal-normalizer.ts</code></td><td><code>normalizeTemporal()</code></td><td>Resolution Accuracy: 94.1%. IST +05:30 offset.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Change Engine</td><td><code>lib/intelligence/change-intelligence.ts</code></td><td><code>detectNoticeRelation()</code></td><td>5-way Accuracy: 76.9%. Audit diff logging.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Priority Engine</td><td><code>lib/intelligence/priority-engine.ts</code></td><td><code>calculateAcademicPriority()</code></td><td>100% Additive Score Invariance.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Workload Radar</td><td><code>lib/intelligence/workload-engine.ts</code></td><td><code>computeWorkloadSummary()</code></td><td>100% completed/cancelled exclusion.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Adaptive Notifier</td><td><code>lib/intelligence/notification-scheduler.ts</code></td><td><code>scheduleNotification()</code></td><td>Enforces quiet hours (22:00-07:00 IST).</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Faculty Portal</td><td><code>app/api/faculty-dashboard/route.ts</code></td><td><code>GET()</code></td><td>Prisma-authenticated course scoping.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Rubric Store</td><td><code>lib/intelligence/rubric-store.ts</code></td><td><code>validateCriteria()</code></td><td>Ensures criterion weight sum == 100%.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Gemini Evaluator</td><td><code>lib/ai/gemini-evaluator.ts</code></td><td><code>evaluateStudentSubmission()</code></td><td>IPv4 forced client; transparent fallback.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Deterministic Fallback</td><td><code>lib/faculty-review/deterministic-evaluator.ts</code></td><td><code>evaluateDeterministically()</code></td><td>100% offline uptime; quotes document text.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>4. Database Referential Schema</h2>
<p>The SQLite database (<code>prisma/dev.db</code>) contains 89 users (83 students including 75 synthetic cohort members + 6 faculty instructors), 9 engineering courses, 211 verified course enrollments, and 89 task records with evidence links.</p>

